ier of bavaria marco suda  said that this week is the week of truth  that they need to be that people need to  reduce their contact and also with new  measures that are in place starting  today there will be a so-called 2g rule  meaning that people who are either fully  vaccinated or recovered from covet 19  will be able to go to restaurants inside  or outside and also to hotels and there  will also be other measures for example  for the christmas market that you can  see just behind me they're setting up  and preparing everything there will be  parts of this christmas market where  only people who fully have been  vaccinated or recovered from the virus  will be able to visit  so that's why they are trying also to  reduce  movement and their calls growing they  say that this christmas market should  even be cancelled considering the high  number of new infections here in bavaria  and how did the situation escalate in  this manner  to me i think there are several reasons  for that when we look not only in  bavaria but also in germany so on one  side we have the vaccination rate that  less than 70 percent have been fully  vaccinated against covet 19 in germany  then of course we have the seasonal  aspect of winter temperatures now four  degrees here in munich meaning that many  people stay indoors with the risk of an  infection is definitely higher then we  have a patchwork of restrictions in  germany with some states  going with this 2g versions and others  taking a 3g  approach meaning that people who have a  negative test can also go to restaurants  or indoor places  several health experts have been warning  for this situation but politicians also  let's remember that we had elections in  september said that it's fear-mongering  promised that there would not be a  lockdown so there are several reasons to  explain that as a some health experts  say the only surprise is that people are  actually surprised by the critical  situation in germany right now  okay thank yo